# b28 — reserved label names at the range step (issue #507): `__error__`,
# `__error_details__`, `__preserve_error__` and `__variant__`, from a field
# in the line, structured metadata, a stream label or a query step.
#
# Reference of record: grafana/loki:3.7.4 (revision b318f282, digest
# sha256:87f0a067673756a3cede1bcbf0c74875f7df9b09fddb53e399d0c576f756cfcc)
# on `ci/logql/config-463.yaml`, the shared config with level discovery off,
# so no `detected_level` pair joins any label set. Captured 2026-09-14 by push
# and query: each stream pushed with `service=<id>`, its entries at T0 (1 ms
# apart), instant queries at T0 + 60 s, the range row from T0 to T0 + 180 s
# step 60 s. The reference derives `service_name` from `service`; the load
# blocks below carry both.
#
# THE MODEL, read at the pinned tag and then measured (ledger row
# `reserved-names-at-the-range-step`, docs/api.md §2):
#
#   R1  A `sum` directly above `count_over_time`, `bytes_over_time`, `rate`,
#       `bytes_rate` or `sum_over_time` with no grouping of its own hands its
#       grouping to the range step, so a `__error__` label that is not the
#       engine's error (a stream label, a parsed field) is gone before the
#       check unless the grouping keeps it.
#   R2  A series whose `__preserve_error__` is exactly `true` passes the
#       check; a preserved failed conversion contributes 0.
#   R3  With the parser hints in force and `__error__` required, a parser
#       error also writes `__preserve_error__="true"`.
#   R4  With the hints in force and `__preserve_error__` not required, the
#       implicit parsers do not extract a line key of that name.
#
# Each section is one row of issue #507's revision 9 tables, named in the
# comment above its `load`. `eval_fail` rows match the reference's status;
# the message wording is never matched, only the error class.
#
# Not expressible here, and so not in this file: the kept table's label-
# endpoint and series rows (c01.11, c01.13), `absent_over_time` over a
# stream that does not exist (d03.02; this runner does not apply
# selectors), and b08's log query (stream label `__error__="s"` with
# metadata `__error__="m"`; streams evals are structured-metadata-blind in
# this runner). The live test
# `query_log_gates::reserved_names_answer_as_the_reference_on_every_metric_route`
# carries the metric rows through the real engine.
#
# provenance: captured
# (file default; see logqltest/PROVENANCE.md §provenance markers.
#  A row may override it with its own `# provenance:` line.)

# c01.03
load
  {__error__="s", service="c01", service_name="c01"}
  0s  {"latency":5}

eval instant at 60s sum by (service_name) (count_over_time({service="c01"} [5m]))
  {service_name="c01"} 1

clear

